    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vikings">Viking</a> settlement on the lower Seine, granted to Rollo in 911, that became a French duchy ruled from Rouen.</li><li>Its dukes kept unusually firm control over castles, barons and the Church, and its abbeys such as Bec led European learning.</li><li>Duke William conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#england">England</a> in 1066; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a> annexed the duchy in 1204.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Channel Islands are the last part of the old Duchy of Normandy still held by the British crown, and their law still rests partly on Norman custom.</p></aside>
    </section>

